<h2>Exporting everything</h2>
<p>The owner can download all of the shop's data from <strong>Settings → Your data</strong>: products, stock, sales, customers, suppliers, purchases and more, as CSV files (they open in Excel or Google Sheets) in one ZIP file. HardPoint emails a link when it's ready; the link works for 7 days. Export works even while the shop is read-only.</p>

<h2>Closing your account</h2>
<p>The owner can close the shop from the same page, confirming with their password. From then on the shop is read-only and only owners can sign in, and <strong>30 days later</strong> its data is deleted for good. Until then an owner can change their mind and cancel the closure from the same page.</p>
<p>Export your data first: once it's deleted, it can't be recovered. HardPoint keeps the invoices it issued to your shop, because tax law requires it.</p>
